# Yosys ASIC Synthesis Estimation Script Template
# Target: TSMC 28nm (approximated via NanGate45 / FreePDK45)
# Usage: yosys -s synth_{{MODULE}}.ys | tee syn/reports/{{MODULE}}_synth.txt
#
# PREREQUISITE: SDC must be generated BEFORE running this script
# PREREQUISITE: sv2v conversion must be done BEFORE running this script
#   sv2v rtl/common/*.sv rtl/{{MODULE}}/*.sv -o rtl/{{MODULE}}/{{MODULE}}_v2v.v
#   (always include rtl/common/ for SRAM wrappers and shared utilities)

# ============================================================
# Read RTL (sv2v-converted Verilog — NOT .sv)
# ============================================================
# Include common wrappers (sram_sp, sram_tp, etc.) + module-specific files
# sv2v merges all inputs into a single .v file
read_verilog rtl/{{MODULE}}/{{MODULE}}_v2v.v

# ============================================================
# Elaboration & Optimization
# ============================================================
hierarchy -check -top {{MODULE}}
proc; opt; fsm; opt

# ============================================================
# Memory Handling
# ============================================================
# memory pass converts behavioral memory arrays to $mem cells,
# then maps to FF or inferred BRAM depending on size.
# SRAM wrappers (sram_sp/sram_tp) should infer as memory blocks.
# Use -nomap to inspect $mem cells before technology mapping:
#   memory -nomap; stat    (debug: check memory inference)
memory; opt

# ============================================================
# Technology Mapping (NanGate45 — TSMC 28nm proxy)
# ============================================================
# NanGate45 is the DEFAULT liberty for PPA estimation.
# To use a different liberty: run_syn.sh --liberty <path> generates
# a dynamic script with your library. This template is for direct
# Yosys invocation with NanGate45 only.
techmap; opt
dfflibmap -liberty NangateOpenCellLibrary_typical.lib
abc -liberty NangateOpenCellLibrary_typical.lib
clean

# ============================================================
# Statistics — Area in NAND2-FO2 Gate Equivalents
# ============================================================
# stat -liberty reports "Chip area" in um2
# Gate count = Chip area / 0.798 (NAND2X1 area in NanGate45)
stat -liberty NangateOpenCellLibrary_typical.lib

# ============================================================
# Post-Synthesis Checks
# ============================================================

# Check for combinational loops
scc -max_depth 10

# Check for inferred latches (MUST be zero)
# $_DLATCH_* in stat output → HARD FAIL

# Export netlist (optional — only when user requests full synthesis)
# write_verilog syn/netlist/{{MODULE}}_netlist.v
# write_json syn/reports/{{MODULE}}_synth.json
